# WeBuy React patterns

- Feature modules over flat component dumps as domains grow.
- **Feature layout (required):**
  ```text
  features/<domain>/
    index.tsx              # page/section UI (named export)
    types.ts | schema.ts | constants.ts   # as needed
    hooks/use-*.ts         # logic only
    components/<name>/
      index.tsx            # nested UI (named export)
      hooks/               # logic for that component
  ```
- Separate UI from logic: thin `index.tsx`, hooks own data/side effects.
- Always `export const ComponentName` — never `export default` in `features/` or shared `components/` (Next `app/` pages/layouts are the exception).
- Keep files ≤ **500** lines (ESLint `max-lines`).
- Colocate component + hook when the hook serves one UI; promote to shared only when reused.
- Prefer server components / server data on the storefront when they fit; use TanStack Query for client cache needs.
- Zustand for light client UI/session state — not a second server cache.
- Strict TypeScript; no `any` without a written justification in the PR.
- Loading / empty / error states are required for user-facing async UI.
- Reuse `@webuy/tailwind-config` tokens; avoid one-off color hex when a token exists.
